  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Neon message intercept",
    "overview": "Email Guardian uses the user-pinned cyberpunk/glitch world: a void-black ground, neon signals, angular technical frames and terminal typography. Green leads actions, cyan carries analysis and magenta creates interruptions. The visual energy supports a school demonstration whose text input and two model outputs remain clear.\n\nThe materials are made in code: a faint grid, SVG noise, CRT scanlines, outlined icons and chamfered frames. Occasional headline corruption, a terminal cursor and slow border emission provide atmosphere. The shared pause control stops animations across both surfaces, and the system reduced-motion preference removes animation and reduces transitions.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Mandatory dark surfaces with green, magenta and cyan signals.",
      "Orbitron headings, JetBrains Mono reading text and Share Tech Mono labels.",
      "Chamfered frames, thin borders and restrained neon emission.",
      "Readable supporting text, visible focus and text-backed result semantics.",
      "Code-native textures and stoppable motion; no shipping raster imagery."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "Readable Signal",
        "body": "Use muted-foreground for supporting reading text and placeholders. Keep dim for decorative use only; it is not the reading-text color.",
